  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Infernal Bulwark",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2327609-infernal-bulwark"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat, introduced in “D&D Beyond Drops”, builds in your infernal pact to make your character durable and unpleasant to touch. Two sources of retaliatory damage and Unarmored Defense from a feat feels great at first glance, but the feat’s features work for a very small subset of classes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Paladins and Warlocks are the most likely to find this feat useful since they can build around Constitution and Charisma exclusively, and will find the AC and Armor of Agathys consistently useful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ablity-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ablity Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ablity-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ablity-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Martial characters will mostly choose Constitution, but Charisma can work for some martial builds and for Charisma-based spellcasters. Not including Strength or Dexterity as an option is difficult for many martial characters at the low levels where the feat’s other features are most impactful."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-devils-flesh",
      "heading": "Devil’s Flesh",
      "sourceAnchor": "devils-flesh",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-devils-flesh-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Constituton-based or Charisma-based unarmored defense. You can get Constitution-based unarmored defense from a level in Barbarian, but Charisma-based requires a subclass like College of Dance Bard. This is a great option for Sorcerers and Warlocks."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-infernal-protection",
      "heading": "Infernal Protection",
      "sourceAnchor": "infernal-protection",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-infernal-protection-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Armor of Agathys is a great source of Temporary Hit Points with some retaliatory damage, but one casting per day isn’t going to get you very far. You’ll benefit from this much more if you’re a spellcaster. If this is why you’re considering Infernal Bulwark, look at Rune Carver instead or multiclass into Warlock."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-infernal-protection-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It’s odd that the free casting changes the retaliatory damage to Fire, but if you cast it with a spell slot you still deal Cold damage."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-vengeful-surge",
      "heading": "Vengeful Surge",
      "sourceAnchor": "vengeful-surge",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-vengeful-surge-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "1d10 damage with no scaling. At low levels this will rarely trigger and you get too few uses for it to be impactful, and at high levels the damage won’t matter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-6",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
